{
  "schema_version": 2,
  "capability": "CORE-PLATFORM-001",
  "comparison": "subset",
  "notes": "watch-publication-disposition uses request_started, attempts, http_response_on_every_attempt, http_2xx_on_any_attempt (missing means false), succeeded and restart_with_sending. First match: restart -> unconfirmed; success -> processed; started and any 2xx -> unconfirmed; started and every response with no 2xx -> released; other started -> unconfirmed; unsent -> released. watch-retain takes ordered keys, optional sending_keys (default empty), recorded_parents map path->{device,inode}, and files containing key,parent,before,fingerprint,after. Missing parent observations are null. Identity components are decimal strings. Apply P5 R0-R5 against the frozen recorded map; output ordered kept keys and the surviving/adopted parents map. A nomination must be stable, fingerprint-identical and unanimous for its parent, and cannot authorize pruning in this write. Expected results are the maintainer policy, not derived from the implementation.",
  "requirement_ids": [
    "CORE-025"
  ],
